        "physicalDescription": "Man's square headdress of printed and wax-resist dyed (Batik) cotton. The pattern is printed from hand stamps covered with hot wax and dyed by the wax-resist process in blue and brown on a buff-coloured ground.\n\nIn the centre is a buff-coloured square 'modang' with a border of in-turned hooks and bands of small repeated geometrical motives. The field (baden) around this is of dark blue. The wide outer border is printed with the 'kawung pijis' design or 'spotted kawung'. Rows of octagons, crossed and enclosing squares and spots in pairs. Inside, projecting into the blue field, is a row of round headed panels each charged with a hook and from which slopes a wavy line.",
